\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces Alive and connected nodes per round (layout 0) until 90\% of the nodes were dead or cut off from the sink. A node counts only while it has energy and a path to the sink; under the FO model every link exists, so the curve counts deaths only, whereas with the CC2420 a node also drops out when every relay towards the sink has died, and the curve can then fall faster than the deaths alone. The dashed vertical line marks LB$_{\mathrm  {LP}}$ on the FND lifetime, and the triangle marks the FND of the bound schedule run as a protocol.}}{20}{figure.6}\protected@file@percent }
